---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
  <SectionHeader
    badge="IMAGE OCR GUIDE"
    title="Everything You Need to Know About"
    highlight="Image to Text"
    suffix="Conversion"
    description="Learn how image-to-text conversion works, when to use OCR technology, and how to get the most accurate results with Hayvex."
  />

  <div class="prose prose-invert prose-zinc mx-auto mt-14 max-w-none">

    <h3>What is Image to Text?</h3>

    <p>
      Image to Text is a technology that converts printed or digital text inside
      an image into editable and searchable text. Instead of typing the content
      manually, Optical Character Recognition (OCR) automatically detects
      letters, numbers and symbols from an image and converts them into text
      that you can copy, edit or download.
    </p>

    <p>
      Hayvex performs this process directly inside your browser, meaning your
      files remain on your device throughout the entire OCR process. No uploads,
      no cloud processing and no compromise on privacy.
    </p>

    <h3>How OCR Technology Works</h3>

    <p>
      OCR (Optical Character Recognition) analyzes an image pixel by pixel to
      identify characters, words and document structure. Modern OCR engines use
      machine learning techniques to recognize text even when images contain
      different fonts, sizes or lighting conditions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Hayvex combines browser-based processing with AI-powered OCR to recognize
      text from screenshots, scanned documents, photographs, notes and many
      other image types without sending your files to external servers.
    </p>

    <h3>Why Use Image to Text?</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>Save hours of manual typing.</li>
      <li>Convert printed documents into editable text.</li>
      <li>Copy text from screenshots instantly.</li>
      <li>Digitize books, notes and invoices.</li>
      <li>Improve productivity for students and professionals.</li>
      <li>Keep sensitive documents private with browser-based OCR.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Common Use Cases</h3>

    <p>
      Image OCR is useful across many industries and everyday tasks.
      Students can digitize handwritten notes and printed study material.
      Businesses can extract information from invoices and receipts.
      Developers can copy code from screenshots.
      Researchers can digitize scanned documents.
      Professionals can quickly convert reports and forms into editable text.
    </p>

    <h3>Tips for Better OCR Accuracy</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>Use high-resolution images whenever possible.</li>
      <li>Keep the document straight and avoid tilted photos.</li>
      <li>Ensure good lighting with minimal shadows.</li>
      <li>Avoid blurry or compressed images.</li>
      <li>Crop unnecessary background before uploading.</li>
      <li>Use clear printed text for the best recognition results.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Supported Languages</h3>

    <p>
      Hayvex currently provides the best experience for English OCR. Support for
      additional languages is planned in future releases to help users extract
      text from multilingual documents while maintaining high recognition
      accuracy.
    </p>

    <h3>Privacy First OCR</h3>

    <p>
      Unlike many online OCR tools, Hayvex processes your files locally inside
      your browser. Your documents are not uploaded to external servers during
      text extraction. This privacy-first approach makes Hayvex suitable for
      confidential documents, business files and personal records where data
      security is important.
    </p>

    <h3>Why Choose Hayvex?</h3>

    <p>
      Hayvex is designed to provide fast, accurate and secure OCR without
      unnecessary complexity. Whether you need to extract text from screenshots,
      scanned documents, photographs or PDFs, Hayvex offers a clean,
      browser-based experience with no installation and no sign-up required.
      As the platform grows, additional document intelligence features such as
      receipt OCR, invoice OCR, business card scanning and document comparison
      will become available while keeping privacy at the core of the product.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>